  }\n   547→\n   548→        @media (prefers-color-scheme: light) {\n   549→            :root {\n   550→                --bg: #f5f5f5;\n   551→                --surface: #fff;\n   552→                --surface-alt: #f9f9f9;\n   553→                --primary: #e0e0e0;\n   554→                --accent: #d32f2f;\n   555→                --accent-soft: #e57373;\n   556→                --text: #333;\n   557→                --muted: #666;\n   558→            }\n   559→        }\n   560→    </style>\n   561→</head>\n   562→<body>\n   563→    <div class=\"container\">\n   564→        <nav>\n   565→            <a href=\"#overview\" class=\"tab-link\" data-tab=\"overview\">Overview</a>\n   566→            <a href=\"#chapters\" class=\"tab-link\" data-tab=\"chapters\">Chapters</a>\n   567→            <a href=\"#characters\" class=\"tab-link\" data-tab=\"characters\">Characters</a>\n   568→            <a href=\"#pronunciations\" class=\"tab-link\" data-tab=\"pronunciations\">Pronunciations</a>\n   569→            \n   570→        </nav>\n   571→\n   572→        <div id=\"overview\" class=\"tab-content active\">\n   573→            <header>\n   574→                <h1>The Great Gatsby</h1>\n   575→                <p class=\"meta\">\n   576→                    by F. Scott Fitzgerald &middot; \n   577→                    Narrator's Guide &middot; Generated 2026-01-18 00:08\n   578→                </p>\n   579→                \n   580→                <p class=\"meta\" style=\"margin-top: 0.5rem; font-size: 0.9rem;\">\n   581→                    Analyzed with qwen3:30b-instruct\n   582→                     in \n   583→                    61m 6s\n   584→                </p>\n   585→                \n   586→\n   587→                \n   588→                <p class=\"meta\" style=\"margin-top: 0.5rem; font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--muted);\">\n   589→                    <strong>Started:</strong> Jan 17, 2026 at 11:07 PM &middot;\n   590→                    <strong>Ended:</strong> Jan 18, 2026 at 12:08 AM\n   591→                </p>\n   592→                \n   593→            </header>\n   594→\n   595→            <div class=\"stats\">\n   596→                <div class=\"stat-card\">\n   597→                    <div class=\"value\">51,257</div>\n   598→                    <div class=\"label\">Words</div>\n   599→                </div>\n   600→                <div class=\"stat-card\">\n   601→                    <div class=\"value\">5h 34m</div>\n   602→                    <div class=\"label\">Est. Duration</div>\n   603→                </div>\n   604→                <div class=\"stat-card\">\n   605→                    <div class=\"value\">6</div>\n   606→                    <div class=\"label\">Chapters</div>\n   607→                </div>\n   608→                \n   609→                <div class=\"stat-card\">\n   610→                    <div class=\"value\">1</div>\n   611→                    <div class=\"label\">Prologue Materials</div>\n   612→                </div>\n   613→                \n   614→                <div class=\"stat-card\">\n   615→                    <div class=\"value\">12</div>\n   616→                    <div class=\"label\">Main Characters</div>\n   617→                </div>\n   618→                <div class=\"stat-card\">\n   619→                    <div class=\"value\">626</div>\n   620→                    <div class=\"label\">Pronunciation Notes</div>\n   621→                </div>\n   622→            </div>\n   623→\n   624→            \n   625→            <section>\n   626→                <h2>📚 Book Structure</h2>\n   627→                \n   628→                <p style=\"margin-top: 1rem; line-height: 1.8;\">This book contains 7 chapters. Chapters have descriptive titles.</p>\n   629→                \n   630→                \n   631→            </section>\n   632→\n   633→            \n   634→            <section>\n   635→                <h2>📖 Plot Summary</h2>\n   636→                <div style=\"margin-top: 1rem; line-height: 1.8; white-space: pre-wrap;\">Elevator boy, a quiet observer from the Midwest, arrives in West Egg during a summer that will irrevocably alter his understanding of ambition, love, and moral decay. He rents a modest house between the opulent estates of East Egg and the mysterious Gatsby’s mansion, quickly becoming entangled in the lives of his cousin Daisy Buchanan, her brutish husband Tom, and the enigmatic Jay Gatsby. Through a series of encounters—Daisy’s hollow disillusionment, Tom’s violent outbursts and affair with Myrtle Wilson, and the extravagant, chaotic parties at Gatsby’s estate—elevator boy witnesses the hollowness beneath the glittering surface of the Jazz Age elite. His growing friendship with Jordan Baker, a dishonest golf champion, and his reluctant role as a confidant to Gatsby deepen his involvement in a web of secrets, lies, and unfulfilled dreams.\n   637→\n   638→The rising action centers on Gatsby’s obsessive pursuit of Daisy, whom he loved five years prior in Louisville before she married Tom. Gatsby, a self-made man with a fabricated past, uses his wealth and grandeur to rekindle their romance, enlisting elevator boy to arrange a reunion. Their emotional meeting at the narrator’s house—marked by Gatsby’s trembling hands, his lavish shirts, and the dimming of the green light across the bay—reveals the depth of his idealism. As Gatsby’s dream begins to unfold, tensions escalate: Tom Buchanan, suspicious and arrogant, confronts Gatsby at a tense party in the Plaza Hotel, exposing his criminal ties and challenging his claim to Daisy. The confrontation culminates in Daisy’s wavering declaration of love, followed by her retreat into Tom’s arms, shattering Gatsby’s illusion of a repeatable past.\n   639→\n   640→The climax unfolds in the Valley of Ashes, where Myrtle Wilson is fatally struck by a speeding yellow car—Daisy, driving, flees the scene. Tom, manipulating the truth, leads George Wilson to believe Gatsby was the driver, resulting in Wilson’s murder of Gatsby and his own suicide. Gatsby, waiting all night for Daisy’s signal, is killed in his own pool, abandoned by everyone except his father and the narrator. In the aftermath, elevator boy grapples with guilt and disillusionment, organizing a sparsely attended funeral while confronting the moral rot of the world he once observed. He reconciles with Jordan, reflects on the futility of chasing the past, and finally understands that Gatsby’s dream—like the green light—was always just out of reach. In his final moments, he returns West, carrying the weight of a story where love, identity, and ambition collide in tragedy.</div>\n   641→                \n   642→                <p style=\"margin-top: 1rem; color: var(--muted);\">\n   643→                    <strong>Themes:</strong> identity, ambition, loss\n   644→                </p>\n   645→                \n   646→            </section>\n   647→            \n   648→\n   649→            \n   650→            <section>\n   651→                <h2>🤖 Analysis Models</h2>\n   652→                <table style=\"width: 100%; margin-top: 1rem; border-collapse: collapse;\">\n   653→                    <thead>\n   654→                        <tr style=\"border-bottom: 2px solid var(--primary);\">\n   655→                            <th style=\"text-align: left; padding: 0.75rem; color: var(--muted);\">Phase</th>\n   656→                            <th style=\"text-align: left; padding: 0.75rem; color: var(--muted);\">Model</th>\n   657→                            <th style=\"text-align: left; padding: 0.75rem; color: var(--muted);\">Provider</th>\n   658→                        </tr>\n   659→                    </thead>\n   660→                    <tbody>\n   661→                        \n   662→                        <tr style=\"border-bottom: 1px solid var(--primary);\">\n   663→                            <td style=\"padding: 0.75rem;\">Chapter Detection</td>\n   664→                       